# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sivan Agreement Vault · environment
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; never commit a real key.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is read at test time. `npx hardhat test` and `forge test` run
# against a local chain and need none of these. This file is only for deploying
# to Celo Sepolia or Celo mainnet.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── DEPLOYER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The key that signs the deployment. It becomes the initial owner of the vault.
#
# Use a FRESH key for testnet. Do not reuse a key that holds mainnet funds, and
# do not reuse your personal wallet: the deployer ends up owning a contract that
# can pause settlement and re-price fees.
#
# Generate one:
#     cast wallet new                      # if you have Foundry
#     node -e "console.log(require('ethers').Wallet.createRandom().privateKey)"
#
# Fund it with Celo Sepolia CELO from https://faucet.celo.org/celo-sepolia
# No 0x prefix is required; both forms work.
#
# A full deployment (vault + allowlist seed) costs 3,120,760 gas. At the
# 52.5 gwei observed on Celo Sepolia that is 0.164 CELO. Measured on a fork of
# the live chain, not estimated. The faucet gives more than enough.
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=


# ── WHO RECEIVES MONEY, AND WHO SIGNS FOR DELIVERY ───────────────────────────
# SIVAN_FEE_COLLECTOR   receives the protocol fee on every release.
# SIVAN_AGENT_ATTESTER  the address whose EIP-712 signature the vault accepts as
#                       proof a deliverable was verified (ERC-8004 agent #9827).
#
# On Celo MAINNET the deploy script REFUSES to run unless both are set. Leaving
# them unset defaults them to the deployer, which puts protocol revenue and the
# attestation authority on a hot deploy key. That is a real mistake rather than
# a convenience, so the script stops rather than warns.
#
# These should be separate addresses from each other and from the deployer.
# Ideally the fee collector is a multisig.
SIVAN_FEE_COLLECTOR=
SIVAN_AGENT_ATTESTER=

# ERC-8004 agent id the attester signs on behalf of. Defaults to 9827.
SIVAN_AGENT_ID=9827


# ── RPC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Celo's testnet is CELO SEPOLIA (chain 11142220).
#
# Alfajores (chain 44787) was sunset on 30 Sep 2025 along with Ethereum
# Holesky, which it was anchored to. Its RPC endpoints no longer answer. Celo
# Sepolia is anchored to Ethereum Sepolia, started from a clean slate, and is
# the long-term testnet. Nothing carried over, so contracts must be redeployed
# rather than reused, and every Alfajores address is meaningless here.
#
# The deploy script refuses to run against alfajores rather than letting you
# wait out a DNS timeout and guess why.
CELO_RPC_URL=https://forno.celo.org
CELO_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://forno.celo-sepolia.celo-testnet.org


# ── TESTNET TOKEN ADDRESSES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to set. The Celo Sepolia addresses are hardcoded in scripts/deploy.js
# because each was read back off chain with symbol() and decimals() and checked
# for non-empty bytecode before being committed:
#
#   USDC  0x01C5C0122039549AD1493B8220cABEdD739BC44E   6 dp   <- primary, listed first
#   cUSD  0xdE9e4C3ce781b4bA68120d6261cbad65ce0aB00b  18 dp   symbol reports USDm
#   USDT  0xd077A400968890Eacc75cdc901F0356c943e4fDb   6 dp   symbol reports USD-T
#
# The script re-verifies all three at deploy time and skips any that does not
# answer symbol(), so a token migrating out from under us surfaces as a skip
# rather than a silently wrong allowlist entry.


# ── VERIFICATION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Celo Sepolia verification goes through BLOCKSCOUT and needs NO API KEY.
#
#   npx hardhat verify --network celoSepolia <address> <ctor args>
#
# Celoscan is not used for testnet: its V1 API now rejects every request with
# "You are using a deprecated V1 endpoint", and the V2 replacement requires an
# Etherscan key. Blockscout needs neither and serves Celo Sepolia.
#
# Verify. An unverified contract is a black box to anyone evaluating it, and a
# verified one on the explorer is the single most useful artifact this work
# produces.
#
# Only mainnet still wants a Celoscan key:
CELOSCAN_API_KEY=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOYING
#
#   Testnet (Celo Sepolia):
#     npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network celoSepolia
#
#   Mainnet (refuses without a fee collector and attester):
#     npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network celo
#
# The script verifies every token on chain before listing it, seeds the
# allowlist in one transaction, then asserts the allowlist actually engaged.
# Without that last check it could report success while leaving the vault
# permissive, which is the exact hole the allowlist exists to close.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
